# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Developmental AI — what does NOT belong in version control.
#
# Context (2026-08-01): the repo directory is 7.8 GB, of which the actual
# source is 4.3 MB. `git add` was once run before this file existed, staging
# 10,000 files (9,393 of them under venv/) and leaving 2.39 GB of loose
# objects in .git. NOTE: a .gitignore never retroactively unstages anything —
# the index has to be cleared and re-added for this file to take effect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- environments / build artifacts ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- SECRETS ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Audited 2026-09-02: NOTHING matching these has ever been committed — every
# blob in history was content-scanned and returned zero credential hits. This
# block is purely to keep that true, because the cost of one accident (an SSH
# key or a tailnet auth key in a public-ish history) is a rotation plus a
# history rewrite, and the cost of these nine lines is nothing.
#
# The CI runner's secrets live OUTSIDE the repo on purpose — in the self-hosted
# runner's own .env, never in a tracked file. See docs/CI_SETUP.md.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ecdsa
*_ed25519
.netrc
secrets.*
*.p12
*.pfx
# runner working dirs, if anyone ever installs one inside the repo
actions-runner/
_work/

# ---- LEARNED WEIGHTS -------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable, and enormous: a single flat-arch skill's policy.pt is ~115 MB
# (three near-duplicate 49250-wide input layers). The pod bank alone is 3.4 GB
# of files that are 0.82-0.995 cosine-identical to each other. Git is the
# wrong tool; GitHub LFS gives 1 GB free, which one skill would nearly fill.
host_repository/data/
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH — DO NOT REMOVE IT (fix 2026-09-02).
# These were unanchored (`skill_bank*/`), and a gitignore pattern with no
# leading slash matches at EVERY depth. So `skill_bank*/` also matched
# `developmental_ai/skill_bank/` — the SOURCE PACKAGE — and all six of its
# .py files were silently never committed.
#
# It hid for a long time because it is invisible everywhere except a clean
# checkout: the dev Mac has the files on disk, and the pod is rsynced by path
# rather than cloned, so both work. Only CI, which has nothing but `git
# checkout`, failed — with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
# 'developmental_ai.skill_bank'` on every suite that imports DevelopmentalAI.
# That was misdiagnosed three times as a dependency/version problem.
#
# The leading slash pins each pattern to the repo ROOT, which is where the
# real weight directories live (./skill_bank_data, ./skill_bank_doorkey).
/skill_bank_data/
/skill_bank_mc_curiosity/
/skill_bank_doorkey/
/skill_bank*/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
brain_backup*/

# ---- run outputs ----
logs/
runlogs/
pod_results/
experiments/results/
runs/
outputs/
*.log

# ...but KEEP the small result summaries: these are the experimental record,
# and they are the reason to have the code under version control at all.
!experiments/results/**/*.json
!experiments/results/**/*.md

# ---- media (heavy, regenerable) ----
*.mp4
*.gif
*.avi
# ...except the documentation figures, which are small and explanatory.
!docs/*.png
!assets/*.png

# ---- local state that should never be shared ----
*.env
.env
secrets.*
*.pem
id_rsa*
skybot_ed25519*
broadcaster_state.json
registry.json
